SecureAuth database migrations

Fresh database:
    flask --app run.py db upgrade

Inspect proposed schema changes:
    flask --app run.py db migrate -m "Describe schema change"

Apply migrations:
    flask --app run.py db upgrade

Do not edit an applied migration; create a new revision for later schema changes.

Existing development database:
If the database was previously created with db.create_all(), back it up first and
verify its schema matches the current migration head before stamping it:
    flask --app run.py db stamp head

Only use stamp after confirming all expected tables, columns, constraints, and
indexes already exist. Stamping records migration state; it does not modify the
schema. If the schema differs, plan and apply a proper migration instead.
